//? Title: Shamir sharing: actual prime-field evaluations and reconstruction ambiguity
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Evaluate a secret polynomial at nonzero field coordinates, then reconstruct its
constant term from enough shares. Actual modular term histories precede the
original secret1234, prime2087, coefficients166 and94, and four three-share
reconstructions.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Over a prime field, P(x)=s+a1*x+...+a_(k-1)*x^(k-1). Distinct nonzero
coordinates yield a nonsingular interpolation system. Lagrange evaluation at
zero is
$$ P(0)=\sum_i y_i\prod_{j\ne i}\frac{x_j}{x_j-x_i}\pmod p. $$
\alttext(The constant term is a sum of each share value times its Lagrange basis evaluated at zero.)
Any k points recover a polynomial of degree at most k-1. Privacy from fewer
points additionally requires independent uniformly hidden coefficients: each
candidate constant has equally many compatible coefficient choices. Supplying
deterministic public coefficients, as this worked example does, is not a secure
sharing protocol. An unrelated output from interpolating two points is not a
proof of privacy; the explicit completion control below shows the actual
ambiguity.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/shamir_secret_sharing_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/shamir_secret_sharing.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::shamir_split_trace(3, 3, {2}, 17);
    auto c = a::shamir_combine_trace({r.shares[0], r.shares[2]}, 17);
    std::print("| actual share index | degree | x power | term | y before | y after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.share_index, s.degree,
                   s.power, s.term, s.before, s.after);
    std::print("\nActual reconstructed constant {}.\n", c.secret);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Field17, P(x)=3+2x");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual share values {},{}", r.shares[0].y,
                                     r.shares[2].y));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual constant from two shares {}",
                                     c.secret));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/shamir_secret_sharing_tiny.svg");
}
```
